      "task_id": "p21-c0-fsm-evidence-scaffold",
      "title": "Implement content-hashed evidence schema and refactor PHASE_ORDER",
      "meta_task_type": "validation",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [],
      "files_touched": [
        "ngv2/fsm_evidence.py",
        "ngv2/transition_planner.py",
        "ngv2/gate_executor.py"
      ],
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "The new file ngv2/fsm_evidence.py is implemented.",
        "Definitions of phase_artifact_hash, advance_gate, ENV_PHASE_ORDER, and PHASE_ORDER exist in fsm_evidence.py.",
        "Refactored transition_planner.py and gate_executor.py replace local PHASE_ORDER literals with imports from ngv2.fsm_evidence.",
        "All tests run with pytest tests/ngv2/test_p21_c0_fsm_scaffold.py -q pass (GREEN)."
      ],
      "spec_author": null,
      "estimated_complexity": "medium",
      "verification_command": "python -m pytest tests/ngv2/test_p21_c0_fsm_scaffold.py -q",
      "spec": {
        "objective": "Implement the new fsm_evidence.py module and refactor the PHASE_ORDER literals in the planner and executor to consume the shared constant, resolving the desync footgun.",
        "functional_requirements": [
          "Implement phase_artifact_hash(artifact) producing deterministic, collision-sensitive sha256 hex hashes of dict using canonical json.dumps.",
          "Implement advance_gate(prev_artifact) which is fail-closed, returning advance=False and terminal='missing_evidence' on invalid/empty/non-dict/tampered artifacts, and advance=True, terminal='' on non-empty artifacts whose recomputed hash matches the carried hash.",
          "Define ENV_PHASE_ORDER as the ordered env readiness 6-tuple.",
          "Define PHASE_ORDER as the verbatim 11-tuple hunt FSM order.",
          "Import PHASE_ORDER from ngv2.fsm_evidence in transition_planner.py and gate_executor.py to replace module-level literals."
        ],
        "interfaces": "Provides ngv2.fsm_evidence.phase_artifact_hash, ngv2.fsm_evidence.advance_gate, ngv2.fsm_evidence.ENV_PHASE_ORDER, and ngv2.fsm_evidence.PHASE_ORDER. Transition planner and gate executor consume this module.",
        "edge_cases": [
          "Deterministic hashing across processes by avoiding id(), repr() of unordered sets, or the hash() builtin.",
          "Canonical serialization in phase_artifact_hash: json.dumps(artifact, sort_keys=True, separators=(',',':'), default=str).",
          "Robust advance_gate logic that never raises and fail-closes on None, empty dict, or non-dict inputs."
        ],
        "non_goals": [
          "No integration with live state machine, worker phases, gates, or stage_command_map in this task. Integration is out of scope.",
          "No modification to ngv2/session_api.py (third PHASE_ORDER copy is separately tracked).",
          "No introduction of clock, uuid, random, network, or subprocess modules."
        ],
        "implementation_notes": "ngv2/fsm_evidence.py is a NEW module -> use a whole-file __JANUSMASK_MANIFEST__ for it; the two edited files use __JANUSMASK_PATCHES__ (replace the existing module-level PHASE_ORDER = (...) line with the import).\n\n# CREDENTIAL-NAMING CONSTRAINT (the AST security gate FAILS the build if a variable whose name contains (case-insensitive) \"password\", \"secret\", or \"key\" is assigned a string literal -- it reads as a hardcoded credential even though this is an external clean-room target with no real secret). NEVER bind a string literal to such a variable. Use a neutral name instead (field_name, check_id, label, name, ident, column) or iterate a collection literal / build the mapping from a list of tuples. This applies to dict keys held in a temp var, field labels, and constant identifiers.\n\n# STDLIB-ONLY CONSTRAINT (the verification environment installs NO third-party packages, so importing one fails collection -> the whole build is rolled back and the leaf is parked). Import ONLY the Python standard library. Import NO third-party package: NO pydantic, NO pydantic_settings, NO attrs, NO pyyaml, NO numpy, NO requests, etc. For data models / config use stdlib dataclasses (dataclasses.dataclass), enum.Enum, typing, and plain dict / json instead of pydantic BaseModel / BaseSettings. If the spec mentions pydantic-style validation, re-express it with stdlib dataclasses + manual checks.\n\n# DETERMINISM CONSTRAINT (the AST nondeterminism gate FAILS the build if it sees a wall-clock or nondeterministic source). Do NOT call datetime.now / datetime.utcnow, time.time / time.monotonic, unseeded random, uuid, os.urandom, or secrets to obtain a timestamp / id / randomness. Instead accept any timestamp, seed, or clock as an EXPLICIT parameter with a deterministic default (the oracle injects it, e.g. via now_fn / make_scripted_clock), so the same inputs always produce the same output.\n"
      },
